      "title": "🪽 Pegasus Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a winged horse, from Cloudsoar to a pegasus called Puffball."
    },
    "intro": "In Greek myth, Pegasus was the winged horse who sprang from Medusa and carried the hero Bellerophon. Today any winged horse in a story or game is a pegasus, and each one needs a name. This **pegasus name generator** makes sky names like Cloudsoar, names from Greek words for wind and stars, and cute names for toys and kids' stories.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Pegasus in Greek myth",
        "content": "<p>In Greek myth, Pegasus sprang from the neck of the Gorgon Medusa when the hero Perseus cut off her head.</p><ul><li><strong>Bellerophon</strong> tamed him with a golden bridle from the goddess Athena, and rode him to kill the fire-breathing Chimera.</li><li><strong>The Hippocrene spring</strong> on Mount Helicon, home of the Muses, was said to have burst from the ground where Pegasus struck it with his hoof. Its name means \"horse's spring\".</li><li><strong>A constellation:</strong> after Bellerophon fell trying to ride him up to Olympus, Pegasus was placed among the stars, where the Great Square of Pegasus still marks him.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Naming a pegasus",
        "content": "<p>Pegasus was one horse, but any winged horse in a story is a pegasus now, and each needs a name.</p><ul><li><strong>Sky names</strong> join wind and cloud to flight: Cloudsoar, Stormsail.</li><li><strong>Greek names</strong> come from myth. Zephyr and Boreas are the west and north winds; Balios was one of Achilles's immortal horses; Aether is the bright upper air.</li><li><strong>Cute names</strong> suit a toy or a child's drawing: Little Pip, Starlight.</li></ul><p>For a horse with a horn instead of wings, try the <a href=\"unicorn-name-generator.html\">Unicorn Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more beasts of legend, see all the <a href=\"../categories/mythical-names.html\">mythical creature name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
